I've completed my analysis. Here's my plan and the changes.

## 1. Analysis & Pre-Thinking

**Core Requirements:**
1. **Sprint board editor** — a modal to edit a board's *name, description, background image and participants (user list)*, reachable from the sprint board.
2. **Board-as-child creation** — when a board is created from the board view, set its `parent_id` to the currently open board.
3. **Multiple active boards** — remove the single `activeBoard` from `src/store/kanban.js` and hold the active board id inside the Vue components, so several `KanbanBoardView` panels can each show a different board.

**Strategic Approach:**
- The `kanban` store is the only source of the "one active board" global state; its board-scoped getters/actions must become **pure functions of a `boardId`** so components own the selection. I verified the only consumers of `$storex.kanban` are `KanbanBoardView.vue`, `SprintBoardView.vue` and `project.js` (`onActiveProjectChanged`). The legacy `Kanban*.vue` files use `$storex.projects.*`, not `$storex.kanban`, so they are untouched.
- Move `activeBoardId` into `KanbanBoardView` data, pass it to `SprintBoardView` via prop, and receive board changes through `@select-board`.
- Extend the shared `SprintBoardModals.vue` with a `openEditBoard(board)` dialog (name/description/background/participants) and a `board-updated` event; wire it from both the kanban top bar and the sprint header.
- Persist `users` (participants) on the board object in the store.

**Dependencies & Risks:**
- `NO_BOARD_ID` virtual board: `boardById` special-cases it so a component can keep it selected even when it holds no chats (the picker still hides it).
- Renaming a board moves chats & reparents children (already in `saveBoard`); the component must follow the new id.
- `newTask`/`addTasksToSprint`/`removeTaskFromSprint`/`newSprintTask` used `state.activeBoard` — now take explicit params (backwards-safe; all call sites updated).
- `SprintBoardView` is rendered *inside* `KanbanBoardView`, so it must not read global state for `boardId`.

**Target Files:**
- `src/store/kanban.js` (Modify)
- `src/components/kanban/board/KanbanBoardView.vue` (Modify)
- `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardView.vue` (Modify)
- `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardModals.vue` (Modify)

## 2. Minimum Changes Approach (per file)

- **store/kanban.js** — drop `state.activeBoard`/`setActiveBoard`; convert `boardChats`, `columnList`, `buildViewColumns`, `sprintBoardChats`, `sprintColumns`, `childBoards`, `parentBoard`, `isSprintBoard`/`isVirtualBoard` to `(boardId)` functions; rename `activeBoard`/`activeKanbanBoard` → `boardById`; add `users` to the board model; make `addBoard` accept `parent_id`+`users`; extend `saveBoard` with `users`; scope the mutating actions by `boardId`.
- **KanbanBoardView.vue** — own `activeBoardId`; new helpers (`initialBoardId`, `boardChats`, `onBoardUpdated`, `openEditBoardModal`); add a "Board settings" button; create boards with `parent_id`.
- **SprintBoardView.vue** — take a `boardId` prop, resolve everything through `boardById`/`sprintColumns(boardId)`; add a "Board settings" button and forward `select-board`.
- **SprintBoardModals.vue** — add the board-settings modal + participants picker and the `openEditBoard`/`board-updated` API.

