| `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardView.vue` | Modify | `props` / computed | Now receives `boardId` and resolves `activeBoard`/`columns` via `boardById`/`sprintColumns(boardId)`. |
| `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardView.vue` | Modify | template (header) | Added a "Board settings" button emitting `edit-board`. |
| `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardView.vue` | Modify | template (canvas) | Passes `:background="activeBoard?.background"` so the board background applies to sprint boards too. |
| `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardView.vue` | Modify | `onSelectSprint` / `onTaskCreated` / `onTasksAdded` / `onRemoveTask` | Emits `select-board`; passes `sprintId: this.boardId` to the store. |
| `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardModals.vue` | Modify | `<script setup>` `defineExpose` | Exposed `openEditBoard`. |
| `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardModals.vue` | Modify | `emits` / `data` / methods | Added `board-updated` emit, `showEditBoard` + `editBoardForm`, and `openEditBoard`/`closeEditBoard`/`toggleBoardUser`/`confirmEditBoard`. |
| `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardModals.vue` | Modify | template | Added the **Board settings** modal: name, description, background image and participants (user list). |

### Quick notes for validation
- **Multiple boards**: each `KanbanBoardView` instance now keeps its own `activeBoardId`; nothing board-related is stored globally anymore (`$storex.kanban` is purely a data accessor). Opening two `tasks` panels with different `params.board` shows two different boards.
- **Child creation**: `addBoard` receives `parent_id` from `KanbanBoardView.onBoardCreated`, satisfying “create the board as child of that board”.
- **Board editor**: reachable from the kanban top bar and the sprint header; persists `title`, `description`, `background` and `users`; renaming follows the active board id and moves its chats/children (existing `saveBoard` behaviour).
- `KanbanBoardSidebar.vue` needed no changes (it is prop-driven); the legacy `Kanban*.vue` files use `$storex.projects.*` and are untouched.

