- When the board view's active board changes, publish the board name into the *app info* (`openApps[tabId].params`) so the desktop `Tab` can render it.
- After the component is created, if the incoming `params` specify an active board, load/apply that board (even if boards finish loading later).
- `Tab.vue` must actually *display* that board name and react to the update.

**Strategic Approach**
- `KanbanBoardView.vue` (the only place that knows the active board) will:
  - resolve a `requestedBoardId` from params/route,
  - set `activeBoardId` in `created()` and re-apply it when boards arrive,
  - publish `{ board, boardName }` to the app params via the existing `$storex.ui.updateAppParams` mutation (the same mechanism `AppWindow.vue`/`AppIcon.vue` already use).
- `Tab.vue` currently reads a *static* `this.params?.params?.app`, which won't react to `updateAppParams` (that mutation replaces `openApps[tabId]`). So `Tab` will read the **live** app from the store (like `AppIcon.vue` already does) and show `app.params.boardName`.

**Dependencies & Risks**
- `updateAppParams` only affects desktop apps registered in `$ui.openApps` (no-op in vibe/mobile, which render params directly — harmless).
- Publishing `params.board` is also read back as `requestedBoardId`, so the last board is restored on reopen — desirable.
- No infinite loop: updating `openApps` doesn't change `activeBoard`.

**Target Files**
| File | Action |
| :--- | :--- |
| `src/components/desktop/Tab.vue` | Modify |
| `src/components/kanban/board/KanbanBoardView.vue` | Modify |

