| `src/components/kanban/board/KanbanBoardView.vue` | Modify | `created()` | After creation, load the board requested via params/route and publish the app info |
| `src/components/kanban/board/KanbanBoardView.vue` | Modify | `computed.requestedBoardId` (new) | Resolves the board from `params.board` / `params.params.board` / route |
| `src/components/kanban/board/KanbanBoardView.vue` | Modify | `computed.initialBoardId` | Uses `requestedBoardId` as the preferred initial board |
| `src/components/kanban/board/KanbanBoardView.vue` | Modify | `computed.appTabId` (new) | Resolves the hosting app/panel tab id for `updateAppParams` |
| `src/components/kanban/board/KanbanBoardView.vue` | Modify | `watch.activeBoard` | Calls `syncAppInfo()` whenever the active board changes |
| `src/components/kanban/board/KanbanBoardView.vue` | Modify | `watch.boards` | Re-applies the params board once boards finish loading |
| `src/components/kanban/board/KanbanBoardView.vue` | Modify | `methods.syncAppInfo` (new) | Publishes `{ board, boardName }` to the app params via `updateAppParams` |

## 4. How it works (flow)

```txt flow
1. App opened  → panel params carry { board?: <id>, app: { tabId, ... } }
2. created()   → activeBoardId = requestedBoardId || first board
              → syncAppInfo() writes openApps[tabId].params = { board, boardName }
3. User switches board (sidebar / board list)
              → watch.activeBoard fires → syncAppInfo() updates app info again
4. Tab.vue     → app() reads live openApps[tabId] → boardName() → tabName shows board name
5. Reopen app  → params.board restored → step 2 loads the same board
```

**Note on scope:** `updateAppParams` is a no-op outside the desktop (vibe/mobile render params directly), so this change is safe there. `Tab.vue` now reads the live app object exactly like `AppIcon.vue` already does, keeping icon + title consistent.

